  <section class="journey shell" id="journey" aria-label="Current checkpoint"><div id="stageRoot"></div></section>

  <section class="sources" aria-labelledby="sourcesTitle">
    <div class="shell sources-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">[ Field notes ]</div><h2 id="sourcesTitle" class="display">History, legend, reconstruction</h2>
        <p>Glass left a letter from the 1823 expedition, but no day-by-day account of his survival journey. Later printed versions differ. This experience marks the broad historical record separately from reconstructed scenes and does not use the film’s invented family or revenge narrative as evidence.</p>
        <p>The route is an interpretive learning device, not a precise geographic claim. Indigenous nations appear as peoples with their own communities and political interests, never as a faceless wilderness hazard.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="source-links">
        <a href="https://www.nps.gov/fous/learn/historyculture/hugh-glass.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Park Service: Hugh Glass</a>
